# Drafted by Gemini (R26 Barrow King), edited. The Barrow King: hook, clues, weakness, the lair fight and the aftermath.

~ arrive
set mf_barrow_arrived
Narrator: Maidenmist's graves stand open to the sky, earth heaped beside each, and a stonemason's cart abandoned at the gate.
check Constitution DC 19 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ arrive_ok
Narrator: You keep moving through the cold, and the creeping weariness slides off.
set mf_barrow_resisted
-> END

~ arrive_hit
Narrator: The air by the barrow saps a hero's strength, and they have to sit down for a time.
damage 3d10 necrotic party
-> END

~ region
Narrator: You walk between open graves, and each one breathes out a thin cold air.
time +60
check Constitution DC 19 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ hook
solomon_roderick [weary]: He says every grave he ever cut a stone for has opened, and the dead are not climbing out, they are being fetched.
set mf_barrow_asked
quest mf_barrow asked
-> menu

~ hook_again
solomon_roderick [weary]: He says there are fewer living in the village each day, and asks if you have found the door to the king.
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask what has been happening -> trouble
* Ask where it comes from -> where
* [if not flag.mf_barrow_found] Ask how to find it -> route_a
* Say we will deal with it -> END

~ trouble
solomon_roderick [angry]: Wounds will not heal near the barrow, the living weaken by the hour, half the village has taken to praying to the dead, and a plague turns the fallen into wights.
-> menu

~ where
solomon_roderick [sad]: He says a king with no name has woken under the old royal barrow, with an army of wights, and the mourners are his.
-> menu

~ route_a
solomon_roderick [neutral]: He says the old graves hold the way down; open the right ones and the king's own stair will show.
* [Arcana DC 19] Exhume the oldest graves for the way in -> a_ok | a_slow
* [History DC 19] Read the grave markers for the king's stair -> a_ok | a_slow
* Dig every grave on the hill until the stair is found -> a_slow
* Another time -> menu

~ a_ok
solomon_roderick [smile]: Under the third old grave a stair of black stone leads down, the rock worn smooth by an army's tread.
time +60
set mf_barrow_found
set mf_barrow_clue_a
quest mf_barrow trail
-> menu

~ a_slow
Narrator: You dig through the long night, grave after grave, and finally the spade rings on a stair.
time +300
set mf_barrow_found
quest mf_barrow trail
-> menu

~ clue
mf_aldous_ghost [sad]: He greets you with a courtly bow that is half a drift, and says he has been trying to leave for a very long time.
set mf_barrow_clue_met
-> clue_menu

~ clue_again
mf_aldous_ghost [neutral]: A short greeting back, in character, that welcomes the heroes to ask again.
-> clue_menu

~ clue_menu
* Ask about it -> clue_talk
* [if not flag.mf_barrow_found] Ask how to find it -> route_b
* [if flag.mf_barrow_found and not flag.mf_barrow_weak] Ask what could hurt it -> weak
* Take our leave -> END

~ clue_talk
mf_aldous_ghost [sad]: He says the king had no name that history kept, only a title, and that his name is carved in lost runes on a blade in the deep chamber.
-> clue_menu

~ route_b
mf_aldous_ghost [sad]: He says if you can persuade him he is free to go, he will show you the way into the king's hall.
* [Persuasion DC 19] Persuade the ghost he is free to go -> b_ok | b_slow
* [Religion DC 19] Say the last rites over his bones -> b_ok | b_slow
* Sit with him through the night and listen -> b_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ b_ok
mf_aldous_ghost [smile]: He weeps without tears, thanks you, and points down the stair to the king's hall.
time +60
set mf_barrow_found
set mf_barrow_clue_b
quest mf_barrow trail
-> clue_menu

~ b_slow
Narrator: It takes a long night of listening, but at the end he lets go enough to point the way.
time +300
set mf_barrow_found
quest mf_barrow trail
-> clue_menu

~ weak
mf_aldous_ghost [sad]: He tells you the king's lost runes: a weapon that bears them is the king's bane, and the king fears whoever carries it.
* [Investigation DC 19] Copy the king's runes onto a blade -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* [Sleight of Hand DC 19] Etch the lost name along a sword's fuller -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* Etch the runes by hand, slowly, a stroke at a time -> weak_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ weak_ok
mf_aldous_ghost [smile]: The runes bite into the blade's steel and glow faintly green, and the ghost shudders and nods.
time +60
give mf_inscribed_blade
set mf_barrow_weak
quest mf_barrow ready
-> clue_menu

~ weak_slow
Narrator: It takes hours of careful scratching, but the runes are finally right, and they hold.
time +300
give mf_inscribed_blade
set mf_barrow_weak
quest mf_barrow ready
-> clue_menu

~ lair
Narrator: Below the stair, the royal catacombs open into a vast hall, and at its end a throne of skulls waits.
* Go in and face it -> fight
* Not yet -> END

~ fight
cutscene mf_barrow_reveals
Narrator: The Barrow King rises from his throne of skulls, armoured in black, a crown of bone on his brow, his sword already drawn.
cutscene mf_barrow_reveals_2
Narrator: Around him the dead stand up, rank on rank.
cutscene end
if flag.mf_barrow_weak
combat mf_barrow_weak
elif level >= 17
combat mf_barrow_full
else
combat mf_barrow_light
endif

~ aftermath
cutscene mf_barrow_falls
Narrator: The King's crown falls and rolls, ringing, and his armour goes to dust; the wights around him sink back into the earth.
cutscene mf_barrow_falls_2
Narrator: Above, the moon turns its gaze toward the southern marshes.
cutscene end
set mf_barrow_aftermath
set old_fears_slain += 1
set moonfall_credit += 1
set moonfall_nights_left += 1
give crown_of_the_barrow_king
quest mf_barrow slain
xp milestone
Narrator: In the Drowned Crossroads the swamplights are already dancing, brighter than they should.
-> END
